---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const effectiveDate = "March 12, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Invoice Americano"
  description="Privacy Policy for Invoice Americano, an iOS invoicing app."
>
  <section class="bg-[#05060f] text-slate-100">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-12 md:py-16">
      <article class="rounded-xl2 border border-white/10 bg-white/5 p-6 md:p-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-white md:text-4xl">
          Privacy Policy — Invoice Americano
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-300">Effective date: {effectiveDate}</p>

        <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-slate-200">
          <section>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">What information is collected</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
              Invoice Americano collects information needed to provide invoicing
              features, including account details, invoice and client data you enter,
              and payment-related details needed to process transactions.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">How information is used</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
              We use collected information to operate the app, generate and manage
              invoices, maintain client and invoice history, process payments,
              provide support, and improve reliability and security.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">Payment processing</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
              Invoice Americano uses Stripe to process payments. Payment card data
              is handled by Stripe under Stripe's systems and policies.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">Third-party services</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
              Invoice Americano uses third-party providers to run the service,
              including Stripe for payment processing and Supabase for backend
              services and data storage.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">Data retention and security</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
              We retain data for as long as needed to provide the app, meet legal
              obligations, resolve disputes, and enforce agreements. We apply
              reasonable administrative and technical safeguards to protect data.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">User rights and account deletion requests</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
              You may request access, correction, or deletion of your account data.
              To submit an account deletion request, email us from the address
              associated with your account and include any identifying details needed
              to locate your account records. We aim to acknowledge requests within
              3 business days and complete deletion within 30 days, subject to legal
              retention requirements.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">Contact information</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
              For privacy questions or account deletion requests, email
              <a href="mailto:reyesasergio@resynctechnology.com" class="font-semibold text-resync-300 underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">
                reyesasergio@resynctechnology.com
              </a>.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
              You can also use our contact form at
              <a href="/start" class="font-semibold text-resync-300 underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-4 hover:text-white">
                /start
              </a>.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
